Here is a Java code that can filter out the songs with the specified emotions and provide a recommendation for a song that matches both deep sorrow and melancholy:
```java
import java.util.ArrayList;
import java.util.List;
public class SongRecommendation {

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        List<Song> songs = new ArrayList<>();
        songs.add(new Song("Song A", "Sorrow"));
        songs.add(new Song("Song B", "Melancholy"));
        songs.add(new Song("Song C", "Melancholy"));
        songs.add(new Song("Song D", "Sorrow"));
        songs.add(new Song("Song E", "Melancholy"));
        songs.add(new Song("Song F", "Sorrow"));
        songs.add(new Song("Song G", "Sorrow"));
        songs.add(new Song("Song H", "Melancholy"));
        songs.add(new Song("Song I", "Sorrow"));

        String recommendedSong = recommendSong(songs);
        System.out.println("Recommended Song: " + recommendedSong);
    }

    public static String recommendSong(List<Song> songs) {
        List<Song> filteredSongs = new ArrayList<>();
        for (Song song : songs) {
            if (song.getEmotion().equals("Sorrow") || song.getEmotion().equals("Melancholy")) {
                filteredSongs.add(song);
            }
        }

        String recommendedSong = "";
        int maxCount = 0;
        for (Song song : filteredSongs) {
            int count = 0;
            for (Song otherSong : filteredSongs) {
                if (song.getEmotion().equals(otherSong.getEmotion())) {
                    count++;
                }
            }
            if (count > maxCount) {
                maxCount = count;
                recommendedSong = song.getTitle();
            }
        }

        return recommendedSong;
    }
}
class Song {
    private String title;
    private String emotion;

    public Song(String title, String emotion) {
        this.title = title;
        this.emotion = emotion;
    }

    public String getTitle() {
        return title;
    }

    public String getEmotion() {
        return emotion;
    }
}
```
The code first creates a list of `Song` objects with their corresponding titles and emotions. The `recommendSong()` method filters out the songs with the specified emotions and then finds the song with the highest count of the specified emotions. This song is then returned as the recommended song. In this case, the recommended song would be "Song F" as it has the highest count of "Sorrow" and "Melancholy".

