public static double calculateAverage(Object[] arr) {
    double sum = 0;
    int count = 0;
    for (int i = 0; i < arr.length; i++) {
        if (arr[i] instanceof Number) {
            sum += ((Number) arr[i]).doubleValue();
            count++;
        }
    }
    if (count == 0) {
        return 0;
    }
    return sum / count;
}
```
This function takes an array of objects as input and returns the average of the numeric values in the array. It first initializes the sum and count variables to 0. Then, it loops through the array and checks if each element is an instance of the Number class. If it is, it adds its double value to the sum variable and increments the count variable. Finally, it checks if the count is 0 (in case the array is empty or contains no numeric values) and returns 0 in that case. Otherwise, it returns the sum divided by the count.
