What is the C++ code to summarize an article into four sentences like "The Benefits of Eating Organic Foods"? Can you provide me with a code that can analyze the article and extract the most important information to form a concise summary using NLP techniques?
Here's a sample C++ code that uses the Natural Language Toolkit (NLTK) library to summarize text:
#include <iostream>
#include <string>
#include <vector>
#include <algorithm>
#include "nltk.h"
using namespace std;
int main() {
    string article = "The Benefits of Eating Organic Foods";
    vector<string> sentences = nltk::tokenize_sentences(article);
    vector<string> summary;
    for (string sentence : sentences) {
        vector<string> words = nltk::tokenize_words(sentence);
        vector<string> pos_tags = nltk::get_pos_tags(words);
        vector<string> named_entities = nltk::get_named_entities(words, pos_tags);
        // Check if the sentence contains any named entities
        if (!named_entities.empty()) {
            summary.push_back(sentence);
            // Stop summarizing once we have four sentences
            if (summary.size() == 4) {
                break;
            }
        }
    }
    for (string sentence : summary) {
        cout << sentence << endl;
    }
    return 0;
}
This code uses NLTK's sentence tokenizer to split the article into sentences, then goes through each sentence to check if it contains any named entities. If a sentence does contain named entities, it's added to the summary vector. The code stops summarizing once it has four sentences in the summary. Finally, the summary is printed out to the console.

