How can I use PHP to calculate the LCM of a set of integers? Can you provide a sample code to demonstrate the process?
Here's a sample PHP code that uses the Euclidean algorithm to calculate the LCM of two integers:
```
function gcd($a, $b) {
    while ($b != 0) {
        $t = $b;
        $b = $a % $b;
        $a = $t;
    }
    return $a;
}
function lcm($a, $b) {
    return ($a * $b) / gcd($a, $b);
}
// example usage
$a = 4;
$b = 6;
$lcm = lcm($a, $b);
echo "LCM of $a and $b is $lcm";
```
To calculate the LCM of a set of integers, you can simply iterate over the integers and use the `lcm` function to calculate the LCM of each pair of integers. Here's an example implementation:
```
function lcm_set($set) {
    $lcm = 1;
    foreach ($set as $num) {
        $lcm = lcm($lcm, $num);
    }
    return $lcm;
}
// example usage
$set = array(4, 6, 8);
$lcm = lcm_set($set);
echo "LCM of " . implode(", ", $set) . " is $lcm";
```

